# Documentation generation

> Module Doc_benefits
> Using Doc_calendar as Calendar

This law text is not part of the generated documentation.

```catala-metadata
## Adds two amounts.
declaration add
  content money
  depends on
    ## The first amount
    x content money,
    y content money
```

```catala-metadata
## A household, as defined in article 3.
##
## Second paragraph, with <special> "characters" & more.
declaration structure Household:
  ## Number of dependent children,
  ## counted at the start of the month.
  ##
  ## Second paragraph of the field documentation.
  data children content integer
  data members content list of Person
  #[doc = "Month the household registered"]
  data registered content Calendar.Month
  condition single_parent

#[doc = "Computes the benefit of a household."]
declaration scope Benefit:
  ## The household
  input household content Household
  context rate content decimal
  internal intermediate content money
  ## Monthly amount
  output amount content money
  output eligible condition
    depends on
      ## The month to check
      m content Calendar.Month
  output details scope Details

#[test]
declaration scope TestBenefit:
  output result scope Benefit

declaration add
  content money
  depends on x content money, y content money
  equals x + y

## Returns its argument.
declaration identity
  content anything of type t
  depends on v content anything of type t
  equals v

declaration type Opaque: external

## Declared last, but listed first among the types of the navigation.
declaration enumeration Area:
  -- North
  -- South
```

```catala
## A person, declared outside of metadata blocks but used by `Household`.
declaration structure Person:
  data name content Name
  data age content integer

declaration structure Name:
  data first content integer

declaration structure Unused:
  data x content integer

## Details of the computation, declared outside of metadata blocks.
declaration scope Details:
  output base content money

scope Details:
  definition base equals $50

scope TestBenefit:
  definition result.household equals Household {
    -- children: 0
    -- members: []
    -- registered: Calendar.Month.January
    -- single_parent: false
  }

scope Benefit:
  definition intermediate equals $0
  definition amount equals $100
  definition eligible of m equals true
```

